    "workedExample": "Follow a gradient by hand. Step 1: pick a tiny dataset and define the loss as mean squared error. Step 2: choose two candidate weights, compute the loss for each and tabulate them. Step 3: compute the gradient — the slope of the loss with respect to the weight — and note its sign. Step 4: take a small step in the opposite direction, recompute the loss and confirm it fell. Repeat once; you have just run gradient descent, the mathematics behind model training.",
    "commonMistakes": [
      "Treating a p-value as the probability the hypothesis is true",
      "Assuming the mean works for skewed data"
    ],
